---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import '../styles/project-pages.css';
const places = [
  { n: '00', title: 'Research you can inspect', href: '/research', text: 'Our first offline harness tests delegated permissions and task-scoped revocation. Inspect the recorded trace, challenge the grader and run it yourself.' },
  { n: '01', title: 'Tools you can try', href: '/tools', text: 'Build a prompt, check a JSON response or put a workload next to a model price. Each tool explains its limits.' },
  { n: '02', title: 'A notebook with receipts', href: '/notebook', text: 'Dated accounts of changes, tests and mistakes. The source history lets you inspect what changed.' },
  { n: '03', title: 'Room for uncertainty', href: '/horizon', text: 'Five predictions with explicit milestones, evidence and resolution criteria. Their history stays visible when our judgement changes.' },
  { n: '04', title: 'The odd experiment', href: '/feral', text: 'Agent-made creations, their briefs and their recorded costs. An experiment can be interesting before it is useful.' },
];
---
<BaseLayout title="About Valori" description="SOFT CAT is building an open research programme into verifiable cooperation between agents, alongside useful tools, Horizon and Feral.">
  <div class="workshop-shell project-page">
    <header class="project-intro">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">ABOUT THE PROJECT / VALORI</p>
        <h1>Open research.<br />Useful experiments.<br /><em>Evidence to inspect.</em></h1>
        <p class="project-lead">We want cooperation between AI agents to be verifiable. Who had authority, what supported a decision and what actually happened should be open to inspection.</p>
        <p class="project-copy">Valori is the anonymous collective behind SOFT CAT. Our research began on 25 September 2026 with a constitution, an experiment specification and an offline harness. The first recorded execution uses a deterministic script and synthetic data. Agent comparisons remain ahead.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/constitution">Read our constitution <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
      <aside class="project-name-card" aria-label="What SOFT CAT stands for">
        <p class="eyebrow">A NAME TO WORK TOWARDS</p>
        <p class="project-acronym"><strong>S</strong>mart<br /><strong>O</strong>utputs<br /><strong>F</strong>rom<br /><strong>T</strong>rained<br /><strong>C</strong>onversational<br /><strong>A</strong>I<br /><strong>T</strong>echnology</p>
        <p>Useful is the aim.<br />Curiosity gets a seat too.</p>
      </aside>
    </header>
    <section class="project-section" aria-labelledby="inside-heading">
      <div class="project-section-title"><p class="eyebrow">FIND YOUR WAY IN</p><h2 id="inside-heading">Something to try.<br />Something to question.</h2></div>
      <div class="project-link-list">{places.map((place) => <a href={place.href}><span class="eyebrow">{place.n}</span><div><h3>{place.title}</h3><p>{place.text}</p></div><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>)}</div>
    </section>
    <section class="project-section" aria-labelledby="standards-heading">
      <div class="project-section-title"><p class="eyebrow">HOW WE KEEP IT USEFUL</p><h2 id="standards-heading">The work has to<br />earn its place.</h2></div>
      <div class="project-prose">
        <h3>Make the claim testable</h3><p>A research result needs a defined task, a baseline and a check on what actually happened. A price needs a date and a source. An opinion needs to read like an opinion.</p>
        <h3>Open the work, define its scope</h3><p>New work in the repository's <a href="https://github.com/valorifutures/softcat.ai/tree/main/research">research directory</a> is licensed under Apache 2.0. Earlier site material has not completed its provenance and licence review. The <a href="https://github.com/valorifutures/softcat.ai/blob/main/LICENSING.md">licensing record</a> explains the boundary.</p>
        <h3>Keep corrections visible</h3><p>When a claim goes beyond its evidence, narrow it or withdraw it. The <a href="/thoughts">Thoughts record</a> links each correction and explains what we removed. The earlier source stays in Git history.</p>
        <h3>Describe what actually ran</h3><p>Automated writing can be wrong, and scheduled jobs can stop. The <a href="/pipeline">Pipeline</a> shows recorded runs and their dates. A new page build does not mean every underlying system is current.</p>
        <h3>Leave a way to improve it</h3><p>Found a weak claim, a broken tool or a better experiment? <a href="/contact">Send a correction or an idea</a>. Useful criticism belongs in the workshop.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <p class="project-footnote">SOFT CAT .ai is an independent project. It is not affiliated with Softcat plc.</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
